# Subresource-integrity hash of the UNCOMPRESSED upstream asset.
#
# Format: <base64 sha384>  <upstream URL>
# Same role as scripts/atlas.sha256 — a pin that makes "where did this binary blob come from?"
# answerable without trusting the person who committed it.
#
# The file next to this one is the gzip of that asset, not the asset itself: 984 KB against
# 3,544,608 bytes, in git history forever and in every binary. TestDocsUI_VendoredAsset_MatchesUpstreamHash
# decompresses it and checks it against the hash below, so the compression cannot hide a substitution.
#
# This exact value is also the SRI hash Huma pins in its own CDN-based docs handler
# (huma/v2@v2.39.1 api.go:684), which is where it was cross-checked from — two independent sources
# agreeing on the bytes.
#
# To refresh: download the new standalone.js, verify its hash against the upstream package, gzip -9 -n
# (the -n matters: without it gzip stores a timestamp and the committed file changes on every rebuild),
# and update this file, the URL below and internal/api/docsui/docsui.go's version constant together.

tMz7GAo6dMy55x9tLFtH+sHtogji6Scmb+feBR31TAHmvSPRUTboK9H3M5NFaP4R  https://unpkg.com/@scalar/api-reference@1.44.20/dist/browser/standalone.js
